  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme Estimate - Civil service Reform with HRMO/PSC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The overall development objective of the EU support for governance sector and therefore this programme estimate (Civil Service Reform Component) is intended to contribute is: strengthened democracy and governance. The purpose of the EU Governance Project (Civil Service Reform Component), is civil service institutional capacity is improved, human and financial resources of the civil service are improved and public service delivery enhanced. The expected results from the activities carried out over the period covered by this programme estimate are: 1.Legal revision and organizational capacity assessment are available, including on gender equality, and mandates of institutions streamlined. 2.Improved levels of skills, competence, performance and public service delivery of Civil/Public Service both at central/local level, including improved gender equality. Sustainable M&amp;E mechanisms are in place in the Civil Service management. There are two beneficiary institutions (BIs) under the Civil Service Reform Component of the EU Governance Project viz. the PSC and the HRMO. The Action Document stipulates following two main activities for the Civil Service Component; 1.(Activity # 3.1) Support to Institutional Strengthening and Legislative Assessment and 2.(Activity # 3.2) Support to Capacity Building and Training &lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
